 r←StormSignature error;line;location
⍝ Returns the signature the storm guard keys on: the error number and the place where the error
⍝ occurred, for example "11 Foo[6]".\\
⍝ `error` is a copy of `⎕DMX`. The place is taken from the second line of its `DM`; it is empty
⍝ when the error did not occur in a function.\\
⍝ `EM` is deliberately left out: a message passed to `⎕SIGNAL` often carries data such as a filename,
⍝ which would give every occurrence of one fault a signature of its own.
 r←⍕error.EN
 line←''
 :If 2≤≢error.DM
     line←2⊃error.DM
 :EndIf
 location←'^\S+\[\d+\]'⎕S'&'⊢line
 :If 0<≢location
     r,←' ',⊃location
 :EndIf
